---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import { SITE } from '../../data/site'

const toc = [
  { id: 'requirements', label: 'requirements' },
  { id: 'install', label: 'build from source' },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'verify the install' },
  { id: 'update', label: 'update' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting', label: 'troubleshooting' },
]
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Install huberclaude — build from source on macOS, Linux & Windows"
  description="How to install the huberclaude CLI from source: requirements, clone and build with Bun, install the huberclaude binary globally, and keep it updated."
  heading="install huberclaude"
  lede="Clone the repo, build it with Bun, and install the huberclaude binary globally."
  toc={toc}
>
  <h2 id="requirements">requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Node.js 22 or newer</strong> to run the CLI. Get it from <a href="https://nodejs.org/" rel="noopener">nodejs.org</a> and confirm with <code>node --version</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Bun 1.3.13 or newer</strong> to build it. Get it from <a href="https://bun.sh/" rel="noopener">bun.sh</a>.</li>
    <li>An <a href="https://openrouter.ai/keys" rel="noopener">OpenRouter API key</a>, plus an optional z.ai key for <a href="/docs/enxame/">enxame mode</a>.</li>
    <li><code>ripgrep</code>: if startup reports <code>ripgrep not found</code>, install it system-wide and confirm <code>rg --version</code> works.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="install">build from source</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone {SITE.github}.git
cd huberclaude
bun install
bun run build
npm install -g .</code></pre>
  <p>
    This installs the <code>huberclaude</code> binary globally. On macOS and Linux, use a
    Node install that doesn't need <code>sudo</code> for global installs, such as nvm,
    fnm, or Homebrew node.
  </p>

  <h2 id="verify">verify the install</h2>
  <pre><code>huberclaude --version</code></pre>

  <h2 id="update">update</h2>
  <p>Pull the latest changes, then rebuild and reinstall:</p>
  <pre><code>git pull
bun install
bun run build
npm install -g .</code></pre>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Old version after update</strong>: your shell may cache the binary path. Run <code>hash -r</code> (bash/zsh) or open a new terminal.</li>
    <li><strong>Multiple Node versions</strong>: with nvm or fnm, global installs are per Node version. Install under the version your shell uses.</li>
    <li><strong>Anything else</strong>: run <code>/doctor</code> inside huberclaude to diagnose the install, or check the <a href={`${SITE.github}/issues`} rel="noopener">issue tracker</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Next: <a href="/docs/quickstart/">run your first session →</a></p>
</DocsLayout>
